---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Button from '../components/Button.astro'
import FAQSection from '../components/FAQSection.astro'

const proFaqs = [
    {
        question: 'Is this a family plan for Vikunja Cloud?',
        answer: 'No — but that exists! Vikunja Cloud has a [Family plan](/pricing): up to 5 users on a fully managed instance for 10€/month or 99€/year, available today, no waitlist. The Pro Homelab plan is something else: it adds Pro features to a Vikunja instance you host yourself. We plan to bring Pro features to Cloud eventually, but that will be a separate offering with its own pricing, not the plans on this page.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Is this open core?',
        answer: 'No. The existing Vikunja stays exactly as it is. Nothing is being taken away or locked behind a paywall. Pro adds new features (like audit logs, an admin panel, and time tracking) on top. All of it is AGPLv3.',
    },
    {
        question: 'What if I stop paying?',
        answer: 'Vikunja itself keeps working. Your tasks, projects, and data aren\'t going anywhere. The Pro features (audit logs, admin panel, time tracking) need an active subscription. The core app you use every day does not.',
    },
    {
        question: 'What\'s the difference between the plans?',
        answer: 'Homelab is a flat fee for up to 5 users, for people running Vikunja on their own server at home. It includes the admin panel and time tracking, but no audit logs and no guest users. Team is for small teams: up to 25 users on a single instance, plus 5 guest users, still without audit logs. Business adds audit logs, unlimited guests, and client invoicing, for up to 500 users across up to 3 instances. Scale is Business without the ceilings: unlimited users and unlimited instances. Enterprise is for organizations that need yearly invoicing, a GDPR data processing agreement, or hands-on support via phone. If you\'d rather not run the instance yourself, a managed dedicated instance is available as a paid add-on on any plan.',
    },
    {
        question: 'How does per-user billing work?',
        answer: 'On the Team, Business, and Scale plans you choose one of two models: set a fixed number of seats and add or remove them at any time, or let us automatically bill for the number of users active on your instance, with no seat management needed. Monthly and yearly billing are both available.',
    },
    {
        question: 'What are guest users?',
        answer: 'Guest users are people you invite into individual projects without giving them a full seat on your instance — clients, freelancers, or anyone who only needs to see their own corner of the work. Team includes 5 guests, Business and up are unlimited, and Homelab doesn\'t include them. This feature is still being built.',
    },
    {
        question: 'What is client invoicing?',
        answer: 'Client invoicing turns the time you already track in Vikunja into an invoice: pick a client and a period, and Vikunja builds it from your time tracking data — no spreadsheet detour. It\'s included from the Business plan up and is still being built.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Can I self-host with a Pro plan?',
        answer: 'Yes. All Pro plans work with self-hosted Vikunja. Sign up, get your license key, add it to your instance. That\'s it.',
    },
    {
        question: 'I\'m already self-hosting Vikunja for free. What changes?',
        answer: 'Nothing has to change. The free self-hosted version isn\'t going anywhere. Pro adds features on top of what\'s already there. It doesn\'t take anything away.',
    },
    {
        question: 'If it\'s AGPLv3, why do I need a license key?',
        answer: 'All Pro feature code lives in the same repo under the same AGPLv3 license. Nothing is hidden or proprietary. The license key activates the features so they work out of the box. You\'re paying for a working product and for continued development of the project.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Does this mean every new feature will be Pro from now on?',
        answer: 'No. Pro features are things that companies genuinely need and are happy to pay for because it helps them run their business: time tracking, audit logs, admin tooling. Regular task management features keep landing in the free version like they always have.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Is this a sell-out?',
        answer: 'No. This is how the project stays sustainable without VC money, ads, or selling your data. Every subscription funds continued development of the same open-source project everyone uses.',
    },
    {
        question: 'How is this different from Vikunja Cloud?',
        answer: 'They\'re two separate products. Vikunja Cloud is managed hosting: we run Vikunja for you, and you pay for the hosting. Pro is a feature upgrade for an instance you run yourself. Pro features will come to Cloud eventually, but as a different offering with its own pricing — not the plans on this page.',
    },
    {
        question: 'What does "private beta" mean?',
        answer: 'It means we\'re ironing out the last bugs before general availability. You can use it in production, but expect some rough edges. Pricing and features may still change before GA.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Can I try before I buy?',
        answer: 'Yes. Every Pro plan comes with a free trial.',
    },
    {
        question: 'I\'m on Vikunja Cloud. Can I get Pro features?',
        answer: 'Not yet. Pro is currently available for self-hosted and dedicated instances only. Pro features will come to Cloud eventually, but as a separate offering — joining the Pro waitlist won\'t get you early access on Cloud.',
    },
    {
        question: 'What about SSO and LDAP?',
        answer: 'Already included in the free version of Vikunja. You don\'t need Pro for that. See the setup docs for [OpenID Connect](/docs/openid) and [LDAP](/docs/ldap).',
    },
    {
        question: 'Do you offer a non-profit discount?',
        answer: 'Yes. If you\'re a registered non-profit, [drop us an email](mailto:hello@vikunja.io) and we\'ll sort it out.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Do you offer purchasing power parity (PPP)?',
        answer: 'Yes. If you\'re in a country where the standard pricing doesn\'t make sense, [send us an email](mailto:hello@vikunja.io) and we\'ll work something out.',
    },
]

interface ProPlan {
    title: string
    description: string
    price: string
    priceSuffix?: string
    features: string[]
    ctaLabel: string
    ctaHref: string
    featured?: boolean
}

// Label stays unbroken so the badge wraps as a unit instead of splitting the phrase.
const comingSoon = (label: string) => `<span class="whitespace-nowrap">${label}</span> <span class="align-middle whitespace-nowrap rounded-sm bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-700 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Coming soon</span>`

const proPlans: ProPlan[] = [
    {
        title: 'Homelab',
        description: 'For homelabbers and their households.',
        price: 'Flat fee',
        priceSuffix: ' / up to 5 users',
        features: [
            'Admin panel',
            'Time tracking',
            'Up to 5 users',
            'Support the project',
            'Email support',
        ],
        ctaLabel: 'Join the waitlist',
        ctaHref: 'https://console.vikunja.io/register',
    },
    {
        title: 'Team',
        description: 'For small teams working in one place.',
        price: 'Per user',
        priceSuffix: ' / month',
        features: [
            'Admin panel',
            'Time tracking',
            'Up to 25 users',
            '1 instance',
            comingSoon('5 guests'),
            'Email support',
        ],
        ctaLabel: 'Join the waitlist',
        ctaHref: 'https://console.vikunja.io/register',
    },
    {
        title: 'Business',
        description: 'For companies that bill their time.',
        price: 'Per user',
        priceSuffix: ' / month',
        features: [
            'Everything in Team',
            'Audit logs',
            'Up to 500 users',
            'Up to 3 instances',
            comingSoon('Unlimited guests'),
            comingSoon('Client invoicing'),
            'Pay per seat or per active user',
            'Priority email support',
        ],
        ctaLabel: 'Join the waitlist',
        ctaHref: 'https://console.vikunja.io/register',
        featured: true,
    },
    {
        title: 'Scale',
        description: 'For companies running Vikunja everywhere.',
        price: 'Per user',
        priceSuffix: ' / month',
        features: [
            'Everything in Business',
            'Unlimited users',
            'Unlimited instances',
            'Priority email support',
        ],
        ctaLabel: 'Join the waitlist',
        ctaHref: 'https://console.vikunja.io/register',
    },
]

const enterprisePlan: ProPlan = {
    title: 'Enterprise',
    description: 'For organizations that need the full package.',
    price: 'Custom',
    features: [
        'Everything in Scale',
        'Phone support',
        'Yearly invoicing',
        'Team training available',
        'GDPR data processing agreement',
        'Managed dedicated instance available',
    ],
    ctaLabel: 'Get in touch',
    ctaHref: 'mailto:hello@vikunja.io',
}
---
<Layout title="Vikunja Pro" description="Pro features for self-hosted Vikunja: audit logs, admin panel, time tracking. For homelabbers, teams, and companies running their own instance. Not yet available on Vikunja Cloud. AGPLv3 licensed.">
    <main class="max-w-(--breakpoint-xl) mx-auto px-4 md:px-0" id="main-content">

        <!-- Hero -->
        <div class="pt-32 pb-8 px-4 text-center">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display text-balance">
                Vikunja Pro
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-6 text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-balance">
                Audit logs, an admin panel, and time tracking for the Vikunja instance you host yourself.
                For your family, your team, or your company.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
                Now in private beta.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Looking for managed hosting instead?
                <a href="/pricing" class="underline">Vikunja Cloud</a> has you covered.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Plan cards -->
        <section class="max-w-(--breakpoint-lg) mx-auto mt-16 px-4">
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
                {proPlans.map((plan: ProPlan) => (
                    <article class:list={['rounded-sm p-6 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 flex flex-col', plan.featured ? 'border-2 border-primary' : 'border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800']}>
                        <div class="mb-4">
                            <h2 class="font-display text-xl mb-1">{plan.title}</h2>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-balance">
                                {plan.description}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="font-display text-2xl mb-6">
                            {plan.price}<span class="block text-base font-sans text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">{plan.priceSuffix ?? ''}&nbsp;</span>
                        </div>

                        <hr class="mb-6"/>

                        <ul class="list-disc list-checkmark pl-4 mb-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1">
                            {plan.features.map((f: string) => (
                                <li><Fragment set:html={f}/></li>
                            ))}
                        </ul>

                        <div class="mt-auto">
                            <Button href={plan.ctaHref}>
                                {plan.ctaLabel}
                            </Button>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                ))}
            </div>

            <article class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-sm p-6 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 mt-4 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-4 md:items-center">
                <div>
                    <h2 class="font-display text-xl mb-1">{enterprisePlan.title}</h2>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-balance">
                        {enterprisePlan.description}
                    </p>
                    <div class="font-display text-2xl mt-4">{enterprisePlan.price}</div>
                </div>

                <ul class="list-disc list-checkmark pl-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1 md:columns-2 md:col-span-2">
                    {enterprisePlan.features.map((f: string) => (
                        <li><Fragment set:html={f}/></li>
                    ))}
                </ul>

                <div class="md:text-right">
                    <Button href={enterprisePlan.ctaHref}>
                        {enterprisePlan.ctaLabel}
                    </Button>
                </div>
            </article>
        </section>

        <!-- What Pro adds -->
        <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto mt-24 px-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-center mb-12">What Pro adds to Vikunja</h2>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-8">
                <div class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-sm p-6 w-full md:w-[calc((100%-4rem)/3)]">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.325 4.317c.426-1.756 2.924-1.756 3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 002.573 1.066c1.543-.94 3.31.826 2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 001.066 2.573c1.756.426 1.756 2.924 0 3.35a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.066 2.573c.94 1.543-.826 3.31-2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.573 1.066c-.426 1.756-2.924 1.756-3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.573-1.066c-1.543.94-3.31-.826-2.37-2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.066-2.573c-1.756-.426-1.756-2.924 0-3.35a1.724 1.724 0 001.066-2.573c-.94-1.543.826-3.31 2.37-2.37.996.608 2.296.07 2.572-1.065z" />
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl mb-2">Admin panel</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        Manage users, teams, and permissions from a central interface.
                        No more poking at the database.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-sm p-6 w-full md:w-[calc((100%-4rem)/3)]">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl mb-2">Audit logs</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        Real audit trails you can integrate with external systems.
                        Compliance-grade, not decorative.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-sm p-6 w-full md:w-[calc((100%-4rem)/3)]">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl mb-2">Time tracking</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        Track time spent on tasks directly in Vikunja.
                        No separate tool, no context switching.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-sm p-6 w-full md:w-[calc((100%-4rem)/3)]">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4.354a4 4 0 110 5.292M15 21H3v-1a6 6 0 0112 0v1zm0 0h6v-1a6 6 0 00-9-5.197M13 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0z" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl mb-2">
                        <Fragment set:html={comingSoon('Guest users')}/>
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        Invite clients and external collaborators into single projects
                        without giving them a full seat on your instance.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-sm p-6 w-full md:w-[calc((100%-4rem)/3)]">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 14l6-6m-5.5.5h.01m4.99 5h.01M19 21V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v16l3.5-2 3.5 2 3.5-2 3.5 2z" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl mb-2">
                        <Fragment set:html={comingSoon('Client invoicing')}/>
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        Turn tracked time into client invoices without leaving Vikunja.
                        No spreadsheet detour.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Still open source -->
        <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-24 px-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-center mb-12">Still open source. Still yours.</h2>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-lg mb-2">Same license</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        AGPLv3. Not "source available." Not "open core."
                        The real thing. Every line of code,
                        <a href="https://code.vikunja.io/vikunja" class="underline">publicly auditable</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-lg mb-2">Pro adds, it doesn't take away</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        The free version stays exactly as it is. Pro adds features
                        on top. Nothing is being removed or paywalled from what's already there.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-lg mb-2">No lock-in</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        If you cancel, the core app keeps running and your data stays yours.
                        Pro features deactivate, but you're never locked out of your own work.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-lg mb-2">Same community</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        Bug reports, feature requests, and contributions work exactly
                        the same way. Pro customers don't get a separate roadmap.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-12 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center">
                <blockquote class="text-lg italic text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                    "I built Vikunja because I believe you should own your tools.
                    That doesn't change because you want to share it with your family or your team."
                </blockquote>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                    <strong>Konrad</strong><br/>
                    <span class="text-sm">Founder of Vikunja</span>
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Social proof bar -->
        <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-24 px-4">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 text-center">
                <div>
                    <div class="font-display text-2xl">AGPLv3</div>
                    <div class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Fully open source</div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="font-display text-2xl">Since 2018</div>
                    <div class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Actively developed</div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="font-display text-2xl">EU-built</div>
                    <div class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Made in Germany</div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="font-display text-2xl">Bootstrapped</div>
                    <div class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Funded by users, not VCs</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <FAQSection faqs={proFaqs} />

        <!-- Convince link -->
        <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16 text-center px-4">
            <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-balance">
                Already using Vikunja at home and want to bring it to work?
                <a href="/convince" class="underline">Here's everything you need to make the case.</a>
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- CTA -->
        <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-20 text-center px-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">Now in private beta.</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-8 text-balance">
                Vikunja Pro is currently in private beta.
                Join the waitlist and we'll be in touch.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8 text-balance">
                The waitlist is for the self-hosted Pro plans above. If you'd rather have us do the
                hosting, <a href="/pricing" class="underline">Vikunja Cloud</a> is available today, no waitlist needed.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center items-center">
                <Button href="https://console.vikunja.io/register">
                    Join the waitlist
                </Button>
                <Button href="mailto:hello@vikunja.io" class="bg-gray-200! text-gray-800! dark:bg-gray-700! dark:text-gray-200!">
                    Questions? Get in touch
                </Button>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
